# Design tokens

- Use semantic utilities from `@theme` in `app/globals.css`: `bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `text-success`, `bg-warning/10`, `text-destructive`, `border-border`, chart colors `text-chart-1`, etc.
- Do not add `text-amber-*`, `bg-emerald-*`, `bg-[#...]`, or other one-off palette classes for product meaning. If you need a new meaning, add a CSS variable in `app/globals.css` (`:root` / `:root.dark`) and map it in `@theme inline`, then document it in `docs/design-system.md`.
- MapLibre paint cannot use CSS variables: use `lib/map-paint-colors.ts` (`mapPaint`) for literal colors and keep values aligned with theme tokens.

Full reference: `docs/design-system.md`.
